From 49961fdcd90b14d7906e5290d95f700b2b2af57a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:06:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs(r57): fold the Fable check's corrections into the report
 and the registry

Five claims tightened or withdrawn, all against this lane's own earlier wording.

"2.4x worse at every n<=8" was the n=1 ratio generalised. The real per-n table is
2.37/2.28/2.17/1.82/1.85/1.78/1.66/1.56 on the head and as little as 1.12x for q5_K at
n=8 on ffn gate/up. Mat-vec still wins at every served width on every shape and type
measured; the margin just narrows toward the boundary, which is the same convergence
section 4's headline rests on.

"The knee MOVES with k" overstated three points. Only k=5120's 16.4% is outside the
5-9% same-config spread; k=2048's 6.4% and k=3072's 2.7% are inside it. What is
established is that the drop is large at the served k and not resolvable below it, with
the transition between 3072 and 5120 UNLOCATED. Still fatal to an issue ceiling.

The n=7 cliff is no longer attributed to R46's NUM_COLS == 7 tail defect. The tree's own
comment at ggml-vulkan.cpp:12194-12201 says R48b's hoist removed that mechanism, and
every receipt here carries route: r48b. It is closer to R61's runtime-class n=7 effect,
at 1.35-1.5x rather than 21-26x and with a constant absolute penalty; mechanism OPEN.
The structural hand-off is that k=2048/3072 never enter the while (num_iters >= 4) body.

Section 4 gains what the decider was actually for: the n=8->9 entry step across the whole
graph, not just the lm_head's +3642 us. The 64 down projections dominate at +929 us
(q4_K) to +2134 (q6_K) each, so crossing the boundary costs ~+0.25 to +0.68 PTE per
verify step depending on which type the down projections carry, and n-max 9 breaks even
only if mean accepted length rises ~23-28%.

Also: the q5_K m=248320 n=8 failure is labelled an ASSUMED R49-class relative rather than
a found one, and the stale IN PROGRESS / pending markers are gone.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-248 R57 q4_K cheaper dot, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: documentation only - no code path touched, no default moves; all numbers re-derived from the committed receipts
Lane: lane-248
Cherry-picked-from: 11ed5b01b (SOURCE PATHS ONLY, ArifiLabs lane-254 R66 integration)
Recut-onto: 1b6185951 (ArifiLabs lane-254 R66c, from 8c9c82510)
